// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
//
//! The build half of the runtime route: four modules and two generated files.
//!
//! An SDK that ships the runtime route calls `createModule` in place of
//! `translate.createModule()` and imports what comes back as its `c` module.
//! Nothing here links the native library. That is the point: in this
//! configuration the symbols arrive through the platform loader at run time,
//! and linking the archive as well would make the linker demand them before
//! `load` ever runs. That also means the `-lm` and, for a `-Dbz2=true`
//! provider, `-lbz2` the C graph links belong to the provider and not here;
//! see `runtime/library.zig` for what the bzip2 closure actually is.
//!
//!   rt        runtime/loader.zig, the reusable core. Pure Zig; imported by the
//!             facade in both configurations, because `LoadSource` and
//!             `LoadError` are this SDK's public types and must be the same
//!             types whichever configuration is built.
//!   library   runtime/library.zig, this SDK's descriptor: the namespaced
//!             synchronization binding, the classification below, and the
//!             load-time checks.
//!   dispatch  generated by runtime/generate.zig from the real translation
//!             output: the table, the wrappers, `load`, and the re-exported
//!             translated namespace. It imports `rt`, `library` and the
//!             patched translation as `c_native`.
//!   native    the generator's second file: the same translation with the
//!             `__root` prologue Aro writes replaced by an import of the
//!             dispatch as `c_routed`, so a declaration nested inside a
//!             translated type names the routed wrapper rather than the raw
//!             extern. It imports the dispatch and nothing else.
//!   sync.c    compiled into the dispatch with `-DRT_SYNC_PREFIX=htscodecs_rt`,
//!             so its symbols cannot collide with another SDK's.
//!
//! ## The one thing a caller must not do
//!
//! Do not link the compiled C archive into a module that imports this
//! dispatch. The facade's `c` import is the dispatch, and nothing else in the
//! graph should reference the library, or the linker resolves the symbols
//! statically and the runtime route silently becomes a linked one.

const std = @import("std");

/// The prefix `runtime/sync.c` is compiled with.
///
/// `runtime/library.zig` declares the same prefix in the symbol names it
/// binds. The two must agree, and a build where they do not fails to link,
/// which is the whole error report: there is no runtime path that could hide
/// it.
///
/// A build that needs a second, independent instance of this SDK in one binary
/// should change this value *and* the prefix in `runtime/library.zig`, and
/// then give the second instance its own copy of both files. Nothing else in
/// the package assumes one instance.
const sync_prefix = "htscodecs_rt";

/// `extern` declarations that the C library provides and that must therefore
/// stay direct.
///
/// htscodecs's aggregate header includes `<stdint.h>` and `<stddef.h>` and
/// nothing else (`include/htscodecs_all.h:93`-`:94`), but the translation
/// step is configured with `link_libc = true`, and Zig 0.16.0's `translate-c`
/// then emits the whole C library declaration surface into the generated
/// source whether the header used it or not. Every name below was read out of
/// the translated `htscodecs_all.zig` this package's own translation step
/// produced, minus the 42 names the htscodecs headers declare.
///
/// **No htscodecs symbol is in this list.** The 42 declared names are
/// `htscodecs_version`, the five `hts_*`, the twenty-three `rans_*`, the
/// five `arith_*`, the two `tok3_*`, the three `fqz_*` and the three
/// `htscodecs_tls_*`; none of them appears above, which is what makes routing
/// the other direction possible.
///
/// **What was observed, and what was not.** The first list was the surface
/// glibc presents for this aggregate, and nothing more. Another libc declares
/// functions glibc does not: wasi-libc, mingw's CRT and musl each have their own
/// additions and omissions. A name such a target declares and the list omits is
/// routed, and a provider is then refused for not exporting it. That is a loud,
/// honest failure at load time rather than a silent miscompile, but it was a
/// real cross-target gap in this file, and it has now been closed by
/// measurement rather than by argument. On 2026-10-04 the pinned translator was
/// run over `include/htscodecs_all.h` for all 53 published cross-test targets
/// and the six check targets; the union of the C-library `extern` declarations
/// it emitted added 533 names this list did not have, and all 533 are below:
///
///   * 357 from mingw's CRT, `any-windows-any` above all: the `_`routines
///     (`_aligned_*`, `_str*`, `_wcs*`), the `_get_*`/`_set_*` invalid-parameter
///     and environment accessors, the `__p__*` global-pointer spellings and the
///     `__mingw_*` numeric-conversion family,
///   * 83 from the BSD-derived libc the generic tree serves
///     (`generic-freebsd`), among them the `malloc_type_*` and
///     `malloc_type_zone_*` allocators, the `cget*` capability family and
///     `suboptarg`,
///   * 73 from Darwin, `any-darwin-any`: `_OSSwapInt32`/`_OSSwapInt64`
///     (`any-darwin-any/libkern/i386/_OSByteOrder.h:59,74`), `cospi`, `sinpi`,
///     `tanpi` and their `_f` forms (`any-darwin-any/math.h:630-643`), the
///     half-precision family (`:645-653`) and `malloc_type_zone_*`, and
///   * 18 from OpenBSD (`generic-openbsd`) and 2 from musl
///     (`generic-musl`).
///
/// Every name in the union is a C library declaration and none of the 42
/// htscodecs names appears in it, so nothing here can de-route a native
/// symbol.
///
/// ### The fortified and alias declarations an optimized translation adds
///
/// The union above was measured with `translate-c` reading the target headers,
/// but `translate-c` reads them under the *build's* configuration, and an
/// optimized build turns `_FORTIFY_SOURCE` on. glibc's `_FORTIFY_SOURCE` block
/// declares a second family of externs an unfortified pass never sees: a
/// `__*_chk` implementation per fortified function, a `__*_alias` redirect back
/// onto the plain function, and a `__*_chk_warn` sibling. They belong to the C
/// library and the C library exports them; `libhtscodecs` exports none.
///
/// This is a measurement, not an argument: of the six cached generated tables
/// for this SDK, the one from the failing configuration routes exactly these
/// twenty-two names and the other five route none of them. That is the shape of
/// a load that passes under `-Doptimize=Debug` and fails with `MissingSymbol`
/// under `-Doptimize=ReleaseSafe`.
///
/// Provenance, in the pinned Zig distribution's
/// `lib/libc/include/generic-glibc` tree:
///
///   * `__fdelt_chk`, `__fdelt_warn` (`bits/select-decl.h:27-28`),
///   * `__realpath_chk`, `__realpath_alias`, `__realpath_chk_warn`
///     (`bits/stdlib.h:23-34`),
///   * `__ptsname_r_chk`, `__ptsname_r_alias`, `__ptsname_r_chk_warn`
///     (`bits/stdlib.h:59-69`),
///   * `__wctomb_chk`, `__wctomb_alias` (`bits/stdlib.h:85-88`),
///   * `__mbstowcs_chk`, `__mbstowcs_nulldst`, `__mbstowcs_alias`,
///     `__mbstowcs_chk_warn` (`bits/stdlib.h:107-127`),
///   * `__wcstombs_chk`, `__wcstombs_alias`, `__wcstombs_chk_warn`
///     (`bits/stdlib.h:143-156`),
///   * `__explicit_bzero_chk` (`bits/string_fortified.h:78-79`),
///   * `__strlcpy_chk`, `__strlcpy_alias` (`bits/string_fortified.h:171-175`),
///   * `__strlcat_chk`, `__strlcat_alias` (`bits/string_fortified.h:189-193`).
///
/// The `bits/string_fortified.h` three are here and not in the pcre2 list
/// because this SDK's translation reaches `<string.h>` and that one does not.
///
/// None of the twenty-two is among the 42 names the htscodecs headers declare,
/// so no native-owned symbol is de-routed by listing them. They are listed by
/// exact name, not by a `__` prefix rule: the generator's lookup is by name, and
/// a prefix rule would swallow names this file cannot see.
